;; Indian chart of accounts — Schedule III (Companies Act 2013) +
;; Ind AS aligned starter set.
;;
;; India has NO single statutory chart-of-accounts with mandatory
;; numeric codes (unlike DE SKR04 / FR PCG / AT EKR). The closest
;; thing is:
;;
;;   * Schedule III of the Companies Act 2013 — defines required
;;     line-items + classification for the Balance Sheet and the
;;     Statement of Profit & Loss for non-financial companies.
;;     Reorganised by Notification G.S.R. 207(E) (2016) to align with
;;     Ind AS (Division II) while keeping the legacy Indian-GAAP
;;     layout (Division I).
;;
;;   * Ind AS (Indian Accounting Standards) — IFRS-converged
;;     standards mandatory for listed entities, banks/NBFCs/insurers
;;     above thresholds, and any company opting in voluntarily.
;;     Schedule III Division II is the Ind AS-aligned form.
;;
;; Convention used here: 6-digit codes mirroring Schedule III
;; hierarchy:
;;
;;   1xxxxx  Assets               (Non-current + Current)
;;   2xxxxx  Equity               (Share Capital + Reserves)
;;   3xxxxx  Liabilities          (Non-current + Current)
;;   4xxxxx  Revenue              (Operations + Other income)
;;   5xxxxx  Expenses             (Materials, Employee, Finance,
;;                                Depreciation, Other)
;;
;; Inside each class the second + third digits group by Schedule III
;; line-item; remaining digits leave room for sub-accounts the
;; customer adds.
;;
;; Tax-account convention (CGST/SGST/IGST/UTGST/Cess/RCM/TDS):
;;   * Output tax (collected from buyers, owed to govt) →
;;     LIABILITY class (3xxxxx)
;;   * Input tax credit (paid to vendors, recoverable) →
;;     ASSET class (1xxxxx) — symmetric to DE Vorsteuer.
;;   * Reverse Charge Mechanism (RCM) — buyer is liable: a separate
;;     pair of accounts so the dual-side movement is visible:
;;       liability  3xxx30+  "RCM payable"  (the buyer owes govt)
;;       ITC asset  1xxx40+  "RCM ITC"      (the buyer recovers it,
;;                                          self-invoiced)
;;   * TDS — Tax Deducted at Source under the Income-tax Act 1961.
;;     TDS payable: buyer-side, withheld and remitted to govt.
;;     TDS receivable: supplier-side, recovered against own income
;;     tax liability. TDS is NOT an invoice-time concept (lives on
;;     the *payment voucher*) but the chart needs the accounts so
;;     the payment-side posting builder can land them.
;;
;; Tag conventions (`:in-gstr1-...`, `:in-gstr3b-...`, `:in-tds-...`)
;; let the GSTR report engines aggregate per-line without hard-coded
;; account-code lookups.
;;
;; Schema fields per account:
;;   :code            — 6-digit string
;;   :path            — hierarchical PTA-notation path
;;   :type            — :asset | :liability | :equity | :income | :expense
;;   :name            — human-readable label (Indian English)
;;   :reconcilable?   — true for AR/AP/Bank/Cash
;;   :tax-recoverable?— true for Input Tax Credit (ITC) accounts
;;   :tax-payable?    — true for Output GST + RCM payable accounts
;;   :tags            — vector of tag keywords for report aggregation

